    "text": "1. Keep the message concise and to the point.  \n2. Use the imperative mood (e.g., \"Fix bug\" instead of \"Fixed bug\").  \n3. Start with a brief summary of the change.  \n4. Include context if the change isn't obvious from the summary.  \n5. Avoid vague terms like \"update\" or \"fix\" without specifics.  \n6. Use lowercase for the first word unless it's a proper noun.  \n7. Separate the subject from the body with a blank line if needed.  \n8. Reference related issues or pull requests if applicable.  \n9. Avoid unnecessary details or explanations in the message.  \n10. Review and refine messages before committing.",
